From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: PS5: no console host for a console nobody sees.

A console program started by a program without a console (a launcher's
tool), or with CREATE_NO_WINDOW, got a console of its own, and with it a
conhost.exe: another helper process, of the seven the console runs
beside the title (process-limit: limit-01, limit-02). Nobody can see a
console on the PS5. Such a program now starts as the session's first
console program already does when no terminal is attached: with no
console, its standard handles as given (CONSOLE_HANDLE_SHELL_NO_WINDOW).
CREATE_NEW_CONSOLE and AllocConsole still make a console, and
WINE_PS5_CONSOLES=1 in the starting process's environment keeps
Windows' behaviour.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/process.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -200,6 +200,16 @@
             params->ConsoleHandle = NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ProcessParameters->ConsoleHandle;
             if (!params->ConsoleHandle) params->ConsoleHandle = CONSOLE_HANDLE_ALLOC;
         }
+        /* PS5: a console nobody can see costs a helper process (conhost.exe), and the
+         * console runs seven beside the title. A console program that would get one only
+         * because its parent has none, or with CREATE_NO_WINDOW, starts as the session's
+         * first console program does here: no console, its standard handles as given.
+         * CREATE_NEW_CONSOLE and AllocConsole still make one; WINE_PS5_CONSOLES=1 keeps
+         * Windows' behaviour. */
+        if ((params->ConsoleHandle == CONSOLE_HANDLE_ALLOC ||
+             params->ConsoleHandle == CONSOLE_HANDLE_ALLOC_NO_WINDOW) &&
+            GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WINE_PS5_CONSOLES", NULL, 0 ) == 0)
+            params->ConsoleHandle = CONSOLE_HANDLE_SHELL_NO_WINDOW;
     }
 
     if (startup->dwFlags & STARTF_USESTDHANDLES)
